Why This Can Be Considered a Scientific Approach
Scientific rigor here does not lie in grandiloquent language or in an attempt to reduce the market to a universal formula. The scientific rigor lies in the architecture's shift from flat heuristics to a formal structure:
features become graph nodes;
connections between features define the information propagation operator;
cells become agents on the graph;
the neighborhood structure is no longer merely an arbitrary geometry;
the quality of the system is measured not only by profit but also by topological metrics;
Adaptation becomes an observable process.
The approach is similar to the concepts of graph neural networks, spectral filtering, and multi-agent dynamics, but is implemented entirely in MQL5. No external infrastructure (PyTorch, CUDA, DLLs, Python server) is required. All the logic is contained within the Expert Advisor.
